{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788313692488659001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bacteroid-computable-vole","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"2895967080284ff427ed3f9a0026b43dd14847f987cc4889e7c3503c4da92d30","event_uuid":"649856d0-799b-4ac5-b622-0b17d55b379d","position":{"commit_sha":"ffa26667ca9a7f79a1518e636f94c91dc5e88f75","position":"1788311582971759001-649856d0-799b-4ac5-b622-0b17d55b379d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"77bf395662678648859bdb5361ec927167be6ca0d96676640507db9d8ccb0da4","event_uuid":"5b71180a-1bad-4a77-a99e-038103064628","position":{"commit_sha":"f625ab2a8da99eb72773b2a5eadfbea01d97c16f","position":"1788311590828084001-5b71180a-1bad-4a77-a99e-038103064628"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788311582971759001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py:319-357` and `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:529-559` duplicate fallback, direction, deduplication, and observation construction. `jira_family/link_direction.py:1-58` records prior one-sided drift.\n\n## Approach\n\nPlace one pure canonicalizer beside the existing Jira-family direction seam. It parses raw `issuelinks`, determines inward/outward direction, handles malformed or unmapped links, deduplicates, and returns canonical link observations. Cloud and Data Center keep separate transports and delegate to it. The provider-neutral desired-versus-observed diff remains unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Jira Cloud and Data Center adapter link extraction\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/jira_family/link_direction.py`\n- shared behavior vectors and adapter delegation tests\n\nCascade flag: true. Recensus semantic, string, dynamic-import, and monkeypatch consumers before moving behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun identical vectors through both adapters for inward/outward links, malformed payloads, unmapped types, duplicates, and empty input.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] One pure Jira-family function owns link parsing, direction, fallback, deduplication, and canonical observation construction.\n- [ ] Cloud and Data Center transports remain separate and both delegate to the shared function.\n- [ ] Shared vectors prove both delegates produce identical canonical observations for all supported and fallback cases.\n- [ ] Provider-neutral relation contracts and desired-versus-observed diff behavior remain unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py","reason":"delegate Cloud link normalization to Jira-family owner"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","reason":"delegate Data Center link normalization to Jira-family owner"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/jira_family/link_direction.py","reason":"own shared pure link canonicalization"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_link_direction_absolute.py","reason":"preserve direction and endpoint contracts"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/jira/issuelinks_map.json","reason":"shared Cloud/DC behavior vectors"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","jira","architecture","rp10"],"ticket_id":"a07a-5eeb-1223-491c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Centralize Jira-family link canonicalization across Cloud and Data Center","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["649856d0-799b-4ac5-b622-0b17d55b379d","5b71180a-1bad-4a77-a99e-038103064628"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788313692488659001,"uuid":"b4f6a06f-b17d-45c7-bf41-20b9d24a505e"}